\title{leeward: terrain wind exposure and campsite suitability}
\description{
leeward maps how sheltered terrain is from the wind and combines that with
slope, water, drainage, and land status into \strong{candidate areas to scout}
for camping. It works on a projected DEM (\code{terra} \code{SpatRaster}, meters) and
a local wind record. Start with \code{vignette("getting-started", package = "leeward")}.
}
\section{Directions}{

Wind directions are degrees the wind blows \strong{from}, 0 = north, clockwise.
Aspect (\code{preferred_aspect}) is the direction a slope \strong{faces}. The two
are never mixed.
}

